345 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (What message does Adrienne Rich want to convey through the poem, 'The Trees'?)
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In her poem, "The Trees', the poet Adrienne Rich highlights the importance of trees and tries to give a message of afforestation. Without trees, the birds would not have a place to sit, insects will have no place to hide and the Sun would not be able to bury its feet \(the Sunrays\) in the shadows. When the trees are saplings, we enjoy the beauty of plants as they adorn the surroundings. But slowly the tree grows. It spreads its roots, its branches and leaves and seems to yearn to go outside where it can live and grow without any restrictions. The trees, then, lose all their beauty inside the house which they decorate.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The trees serve many purposes when planted in forests. They become a space wherein all other natural species of plants, animals, birds, insects etc. can survive. They are welcomed into nature by the strong winds and the moon.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
