358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ("The Trees' is a short symbolic poem focusing on the movement of trees that are initially indoors but seeking to escape to freedom in the forest. The trees represent nature but also the nature of being - womanhood in particular. 'The Trees', then, is an extended metaphor since the trees are indeed people, specifically females who are in need of healing.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Trees normally make up the forest but until now it's been empty for many days and nights. This is symbolic of women being left in the dark for too long not knowing their true identities and where they belong. Thus, there is a struggle for this identity and a new forest is formed. This new forest will take shape very quickly, overnight says the speaker, pointing towards a sort of change in identity, a collective identity for women.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
